        "map": "tideglass_hall_works",
        "x": 2,
        "y": 20,
        "facing": "down"
      }
    ],
    "_note": "A DRAIN IS PALE WATER TOO. It was a puddle tile first, and a sand-coloured puddle in a grey stone tank read as a mistake rather than as a hole -- and worse, it broke the one rule this room teaches, which is that pale water is the stuff that takes you. Two tiles wide in the low corner of each staithe, for the same body-alignment reason the lanes are two wide."
  },
